(THE PURPOSE OF THIS BOOK) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This book is written for the purpose of giving our clients some ideas of) Tj T*
(the fundamental principles that guide us when we select stocks for them) Tj T*
(to buy, but these principles are valuable to every person who trades in) Tj T*
(listed stocks or in any other kind of speculative stocks.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(First of all, we want you to get a clear conception of the meaning of) Tj T*
(the word speculation, which is explained in the next chapter. Our) Tj T*
(purpose is to protect you against losses as well as to enable you to) Tj T*
(make profits, and it is very important that you understand how to) Tj T*
(provide for safety in your speculating.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is a well known fact that there are tremendous losses in stock) Tj T*
(speculation, but we claim that almost all of these losses would be) Tj T*
(avoided if all speculators were guided by the principles expounded in) Tj T*
(this book.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
("What" and "When" are two very important words in stock speculation, and) Tj T*
(we cannot urge upon you too strongly to study carefully Chapters V. to) Tj T*
(IX.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Chapters X. to XV. tell you much about the influences that affect the) Tj T*
(prices of stocks, a knowledge of which should also be a guide to you in) Tj T*
(making your selections.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Perhaps the most important chapter in the entire book is XXV., on Market) Tj T*
(Information. A careful reading of this chapter should convince you that) Tj T*
(much of the prevailing information about the stock market is misleading.) Tj T*
(That fact alone accounts for many of the losses in stock speculation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It has been our aim to state all facts briefly. The entire book is not) Tj T*
(long, and it will not require much of your time to read it through) Tj T*
(carefully. We are sure you will get many ideas from it that will help) Tj T*
(you.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHAPTER II.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(WHAT IS SPECULATION?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To speculate is to theorize about something that is uncertain. We can) Tj T*
(speculate about anything that is uncertain, but we use the word) Tj T*
("speculation" in this book with particular reference to the buying and) Tj T*
(selling of stocks and bonds for the purpose of making a profit. When) Tj T*
(people buy stocks and bonds for the income they get from them and the) Tj T*
(amount of that income is fixed, they are said to invest and not to) Tj T*
(speculate. In nearly all investments there is also an element of) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R >> >> /Contents 10 0 R >>
endobj
12 0 obj
<< /Length 3142 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(speculation, because the market price of investments is subject to) Tj T*
(change. "Investment" also conveys the idea of holding for some time) Tj T*
(whatever you have purchased, while speculation conveys the idea of) Tj T*
(selling for a quick profit rather than holding for income.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To the minds of most people, the word "speculation" conveys the thought) Tj T*
(of risk, and many people think it means great risk. The dictionary gives) Tj T*
(for one of the meanings of speculation, "a risky investment for large) Tj T*
(profit," but speculation need not necessarily be risky at all. The) Tj T*
(author of this book once used the expression, "stock speculating with) Tj T*
(safety," and he was severely criticized by a certain financial magazine.) Tj T*
(Evidently the editor of that magazine thought that "speculating" and) Tj T*
("safety" were contradictory terms, but the expression is perfectly) Tj T*
(correct. Stock speculating with safety is possible.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Of course, we all know that the word "safety" is seldom used in an) Tj T*
(absolute sense. We frequently read such expressions as: "The elevators) Tj T*
(in modern office buildings are run with safety." "It is possible to) Tj T*
(cross the ocean with safety." "You can travel from New York to San) Tj T*
(Francisco in a railroad train with safety." And yet accidents do occur) Tj T*
(and people do lose their lives in elevators, steamships, and railroad) Tj T*
(trains. Because serious accidents are comparatively rare, we use the) Tj T*
(word "safety.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In like manner it is possible to purchase stocks sometimes when it is) Tj T*
(almost certain that the purchaser will make a profit, and that is "stock) Tj T*
(speculating with safety." When Liberty Bonds were selling in the 80's,) Tj T*
(many people bought them for speculation. They were not taking any risk,) Tj T*
(except the slight risk that the market price might go still lower before) Tj T*
(it would go higher, and that did not involve any risk for those who knew) Tj T*
(they could hold them. The fact that the market prices of Liberty Bonds) Tj T*
(would advance was based upon an economic law that never fails. That law) Tj T*
(is that when interest rates go up, the market prices of bonds go down,) Tj T*
(and when interest rates go down, the market prices of bonds go up. When) Tj T*
(Liberty Bonds were selling in the 80's, interest rates were so very) Tj T*
(high, it was certain that they would come down. That the market prices) Tj T*
(of Liberty Bonds would go up was also certain, but nobody could tell how) Tj T*
(much they would go up in a given time. It was that element of) Tj T*
(uncertainty that made them speculative, and not that there was any doubt) Tj T*
(about the fact that the market prices of them would go up. Buying) Tj T*
(Liberty Bonds at that time was speculating with safety. If you read this) Tj T*
(book with understanding, you will know much about speculating with) Tj T*
(safety.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
