(them. It is a well known fact that the great majority of people buy) Tj T*
(stocks near the top and sell near the bottom. Naturally when everybody) Tj T*
(is optimistic, stocks will sell up high, but sooner or later they will) Tj T*
(come down again, and when everything looks very promising is a good time) Tj T*
(to sell. It is better to lose a little of the profit that you might have) Tj T*
(made by holding on longer than not to be on the safe side. The man who) Tj T*
(tries to sell at the top nearly always loses, because stocks seldom sell) Tj T*
(as high as it is predicted they will, or, in other words, the) Tj T*
(prediction of higher prices is advanced more rapidly than the prices.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
