(prediction of these movements.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHAPTER XI.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(MAJOR MOVEMENTS IN PRICES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Stock prices move up and down in cycles. These are the major movements) Tj T*
(in prices, but there may be many minor movements up and down within the) Tj T*
(major movements. These stock price movements nearly always precede a) Tj T*
(change in business conditions; that is, an upward movement in stock) Tj T*
(prices is an indication that business conditions are going to improve,) Tj T*
(and a downward movement in stock prices is an indication that business) Tj T*
(conditions are going to get worse.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At the present writing, we are in a period of improvement. Stock prices) Tj T*
(began to go up in August, 1921. The upward movement has been slow, but) Tj T*
(gradual. In a period of seven months, forty representative stocks show) Tj T*
(an upward movement of about 20 points, although business has not shown) Tj T*
(much improvement. A steady upward movement in stock prices is a sure) Tj T*
(sign that business conditions are beginning to improve, even though that) Tj T*
(improvement is not noticeable.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These major stock movements are not an exact duplicate of any previous) Tj T*
(ones, and it is impossible to tell how long they will last or just what) Tj T*
(course they will take. Certain influences could change a period of) Tj T*
(improvement into a period of prosperity very quickly.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A period of prosperity is noted for high prices, high wages, and) Tj T*
(increasing production in all lines. Everybody is optimistic. Most people) Tj T*
(spend their money freely, and that makes times better. As prices go up) Tj T*
(and business increases, more money is required in business and interest) Tj T*
(rates go up. As a consequence, when interest rates go up, bond prices go) Tj T*
(down. During this period, speculative stocks are selling at their) Tj T*
(highest prices; and under the influence of this movement, many stocks) Tj T*
(that have no actual value sell up at high prices. Of course, wise) Tj T*
(speculators sell all their stocks during this period.) Tj T*
ET
