(increase. When you see these reserves go down to a very low point, it is) Tj T*
(usually time for you to sell your stocks.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHAPTER XIII.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(MINOR MOVEMENTS IN PRICES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Within the major movements of stock prices, there always are several) Tj T*
(minor movements, which are caused by various influences. One of the) Tj T*
(important causes is the technical condition of the market. Another cause) Tj T*
(might be called a psychological one. When stocks are moving up steadily) Tj T*
(in a bull market, people closely connected with the market expect a) Tj T*
(reaction and watch for it. The newspapers predict it. Consequently,) Tj T*
(there is sufficient let-up in buying to allow the pressure of selling by) Tj T*
(the bears to bring it about. However, the desire to buy during reactions) Tj T*
(is so general, many people rush in to buy and this buying, in addition) Tj T*
(to the covering by the shorts, puts the market up again; and if) Tj T*
(conditions are favorable for a bull market, prices will go up much) Tj T*
(higher than they were before.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In like manner, we have rallies in bear markets. Of course the) Tj T*
(professional bears sell during these rallies, with the expectation of) Tj T*
(buying later at a cheaper price.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These minor price changes mean more to the majority of traders than the) Tj T*
(major movements. The major movements are so slow that people get out of) Tj T*
(patience, and yet those who are guided only by the major movements are) Tj T*
(operating on a much safer basis. We believe that a greater amount of) Tj T*
(money can be made, with a minimum risk, by being guided principally by) Tj T*
(the major movements, while taking advantage of the minor movements in a) Tj T*
(minor way. However, stocks do not move uniformly and there frequently is) Tj T*
(an opportunity to buy some particular stock at a bargain when nearly all) Tj T*
(stocks are selling too high. We try to pick out these opportunities for) Tj T*
(our clients.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Reports of earnings by various companies influence stock prices, as does) Tj T*
(also the paying of extra dividends or the passing up of dividends. A) Tj T*
(peculiar psychological influence is noticed when a company declares an) Tj T*
(extra dividend. The price of the stock usually goes up, while as a) Tj T*
(matter of fact the intrinsic value of the stock is decreased by the) Tj T*
(amount of this dividend; and sometimes it is advisable to sell a stock) Tj T*
(shortly after an advance in its dividend rate.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHAPTER XIV.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
