(TECHNICAL CONDITIONS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Technical conditions refer to the conditions that usually affect the) Tj T*
(supply and demand, such as short interests, floating supply, and stop) Tj T*
(loss orders.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is sometimes said that supply and demand must be equal or else there) Tj T*
(could not be any sales, but that is not so. There are always some people) Tj T*
(who are willing to sell at some price above the market who will not sell) Tj T*
(at the market; and when the demand for stock is greater than the supply,) Tj T*
(it goes up until it is supplied by some of these people who are holding) Tj T*
(it at a higher price.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It works the same way when the supply is greater than the demand. There) Tj T*
(are always some people who will buy at some price below the market.) Tj T*
(Therefore, when the supply is greater than the demand prices must go) Tj T*
(down.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A stock may have an intrinsic value of $100 a share and yet be selling) Tj T*
(at $50 a share, and it can never sell higher than $50 until all stock) Tj T*
(that is offered at that price is bought.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(However, you should keep this in mind: if the real value is $100 a) Tj T*
(share, sooner or later the market price will approach that figure. That) Tj T*
(is why we so strongly urge our clients to buy stocks that have actual) Tj T*
(values, or at least prospective values far greater than their market) Tj T*
(prices, and either to buy them outright or margin them very heavily, and) Tj T*
(then hold them until the prices do go up.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Of course, when one finds that a mistake has been made, the sooner one) Tj T*
(sells and takes a loss the better.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHAPTER XV.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(MANIPULATIONS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Stock prices are influenced largely by manipulation. Years ago when the) Tj T*
(volume of trading on the New York Stock Exchange was small compared with) Tj T*
(what it is today, it was possible to influence the entire market by) Tj T*
(manipulation, but it would be very difficult to do that today. It is) Tj T*
(only certain stocks that are manipulated; but if conditions are) Tj T*
(favorable, many other stocks may be influenced by them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There are different kinds of manipulation. One is for the insiders of a) Tj T*
(company to give out unfavorable news about their company if they want) Tj T*
(the price of the stock to go down, so that they can buy it in; or to) Tj T*
