(borrowed the other 80% of the purchase price, you would be buying a home) Tj T*
(on margin. The principal difference is that when you buy from a broker) Tj T*
(on margin, one of the conditions of his contract is that he has the) Tj T*
(right to sell your stock provided the market price drops down to the) Tj T*
(amount that you owe on the stock, whereas if you borrow money on a home,) Tj T*
(it is usually for a certain specified time and the lender cannot sell) Tj T*
(you out until that time expires. However, in principle, there is very) Tj T*
(little difference between the two transactions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Most margin traders do not put up sufficient margin. If you put up only) Tj T*
(the minimum margin, your broker has the right to call on you for more) Tj T*
(margin if the price of the stock declines at all. Unless you are fully) Tj T*
(prepared at all times to put up an additional margin when called upon,) Tj T*
(you should make smaller purchases and put up a heavy margin when you) Tj T*
(buy. The amount of margin depends upon the transaction, but we advise) Tj T*
(from 30% to 50%, and at times we advise not less than 50% margin on any) Tj T*
(purchase. In fact there are times when we advise not to buy stocks on) Tj T*
(margin at all.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
