(By short selling, we mean selling a stock that you do not possess, with) Tj T*
(the intention of buying it later. Short selling in general business is) Tj T*
(very common, and we think nothing of it. Manufacturers frequently sell) Tj T*
(goods that are not yet made, to be delivered at some future time.) Tj T*
(Selling stocks short is a similar transaction, except that in a majority) Tj T*
(of cases delivery of the stock must be made immediately.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(However, your broker can attend to that by borrowing the stock. As) Tj T*
(explained in the preceding chapter, when the market is active most of) Tj T*
(the trading is done on margin. Your broker buys a stock for you, but as) Tj T*
(he has to pay for it in full, it is customary for him to take it to his) Tj T*
(bank and borrow money on it. A bank usually lends about 80% of the) Tj T*
(market value, but if some other broker wants to borrow this stock, he) Tj T*
(will lend the full value of it. If that particular stock is very scarce) Tj T*
(and hard to get, the lender of the stock may get the use of the money) Tj T*
(without any interest.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Therefore, there is an advantage to the broker in lending stock, and for) Tj T*
(that reason it is nearly always possible for a broker to arrange) Tj T*
(delivery of stock for you if you wish to sell short. When you instruct) Tj T*
(him later on to buy the stock for you, he will do so and deliver it to) Tj T*
(the broker from whom he borrowed it, who will return the money he) Tj T*
(received for it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When you sell stock short and the price goes up, you will have to pay a) Tj T*
(higher price for it. Therefore, to protect himself against the) Tj T*
(possibility of losing, your broker demands a payment from you just the) Tj T*
(same as you pay margin when you buy stock.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Short selling is something that we do not recommend very much to our) Tj T*
(clients. We think it is not advisable to do any short selling as long as) Tj T*
(there are good opportunities to make money by buying; but when all) Tj T*
(bargains disappear, as they do sometimes, you must either sell short or) Tj T*
(else keep out of the market entirely. At such times, there may be many) Tj T*
(opportunities to make money by short selling, and we do not consider) Tj T*
(that there is any reason why our clients should not take advantage of) Tj T*
(them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Of course, great care must be exercised in selling stocks short. You) Tj T*
(might sell a stock short because you know the market price is 100%) Tj T*
(greater than its real value, but it is possible for manipulators to) Tj T*
(force it up a great deal higher; and if you are not able to put up) Tj T*
(sufficient money with your broker to protect him, he will buy at a high) Tj T*
(price and you will lose the money you have put up with him. In some) Tj T*
(instances, stocks are cornered and the short interests are forced to buy) Tj T*
(the stocks at prices that represent enormous losses.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is a common thing to read about the short interests in certain) Tj T*
(stocks. All stocks that are sold short must be bought sooner or later,) Tj T*
(and when that buying takes place, it may affect the market very much.) Tj T*
ET
