(CHAPTER XVIII.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(BUCKET SHOPS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There has been so much publicity given to bucket shops, nearly everybody) Tj T*
(is familiar with the term. A broker runs a bucket shop when he sells) Tj T*
(stock to his clients on margin and either never buys the stock for their) Tj T*
(accounts, or else sells it immediately after buying it. The bucket shop) Tj T*
(simply gets your money on the supposition that you are more likely to be) Tj T*
(wrong than to be right. Of course, if you take the bucket shop's advice) Tj T*
(you surely are likely to be wrong. Bucket shops get their clients into) Tj T*
(the very speculative stocks, where there is likely to be a great deal of) Tj T*
(fluctuation in the price of the stocks, which gives them frequent) Tj T*
(opportunities to sell out their clients.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When the market is going down or when there are many movements up and) Tj T*
(down in the price of stocks, the bucket shops make money rapidly, but) Tj T*
(occasionally there is a long period when the market is working against) Tj T*
(the bucket shops, and unless they have a great deal of money they must) Tj T*
(fail.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In August, 1921, Stock Exchange stocks started to go up. The upward) Tj T*
(movement was very slow but it was continual. Up to the time of this) Tj T*
(writing, there has not been a three-point reaction, except in a few) Tj T*
(stocks, in all of that time. Without a fluctuating market, the bucket) Tj T*
(shop has no chance to clean out its customers. As a consequence, the) Tj T*
(bucket shops began to fail in the early part of 1922, and up to the) Tj T*
(present writing \(April, 1922\) there have been more than fifty of these) Tj T*
(failures. However, it is not likely that all the bucket shops will be) Tj T*
(put out of business. The more successful ones are likely to "weather the) Tj T*
(storm.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Many laws have been enacted against bucket shops, and we believe some) Tj T*
(way will be found to get rid of them at some future time; but we do not) Tj T*
(expect that to happen soon, and we warn our readers not to get into) Tj T*
(their hands, because if they do not get your money away from you one way) Tj T*
(they are likely to get it some other way. The man who runs a bucket shop) Tj T*
(usually has no conscience, and it certainly is an unfortunate thing for) Tj T*
(anyone to get mixed up with such a man.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
