(CHAPTER XIX.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHOOSING A BROKER) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is very important that you choose a good broker. No matter how) Tj T*
(careful you are, it is possible to make a mistake. However, if you) Tj T*
(choose a broker who is a member of the New York Stock Exchange, you have) Tj T*
(eliminated a very large percentage of your chances of getting a wrong) Tj T*
(broker.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Occasionally a member of the Stock Exchange fails and once in a while) Tj T*
(one is suspended for running a bucket shop or being connected with one,) Tj T*
(but these instances are very rare compared with the number of brokers) Tj T*
(who get into trouble who are not members of the New York Stock Exchange.) Tj T*
(The rules and regulations of the Stock Exchange protect you to a great) Tj T*
(extent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When you buy stock on margin, you leave your money in the hands of a) Tj T*
(broker, and you should know that he is responsible. No matter who your) Tj T*
(broker is, you should get a report on him. If you are a subscriber to) Tj T*
(Bradstreet's or Dun's Agencies, get a report from them. If you are not a) Tj T*
(subscriber to any mercantile agency, you perhaps have a friend who can) Tj T*
(get a report for you, or your bank may get one for you. Banks make a) Tj T*
(practice of getting reports of this kind for their clients. When asked) Tj T*
(to do so, we send our clients the names of brokers who are members of) Tj T*
(the New York Stock Exchange, but we prefer not to recommend any broker.) Tj T*
(Of course, we cannot guarantee that a broker is all right. We simply use) Tj T*
(our best judgment, but, as we said before, you eliminate a large) Tj T*
(percentage of your chances of going wrong when you trade with a broker) Tj T*
(who is a member of the New York Stock Exchange.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHAPTER XX.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(PUTS AND CALLS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A "put" is a negotiable contract giving the holder the privilege to sell) Tj T*
(a specified number of shares of a certain stock to the maker at a fixed) Tj T*
(price, within a specified time. A "call" is the exact reverse. It is a) Tj T*
(negotiable contract giving the holder the privilege to buy a specified) Tj T*
(number of shares of a certain stock from the maker at a fixed price,) Tj T*
(within a specified time. The price fixed in a put or call is set away) Tj T*
(from the market price a certain number of points, depending upon the) Tj T*
(stock and the condition of the market. When the market is steady and not) Tj T*
(fluctuating, the price fixed is frequently only two points away, but in) Tj T*
(a more active market it is considerably more.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For instance, at the present time, U. S. Steel is selling at about 95,) Tj T*
ET
