70 0 obj
<< /Length 3525 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
() Tj T*
(It is more difficult, however, to tell you WHAT stocks to buy. First of) Tj T*
(all, we advise you against buying stocks that are put up to high prices) Tj T*
(by manipulation. Of course, if you get in one of those stocks right and) Tj T*
(get out right, your profits are very large, but you take a great risk,) Tj T*
(and those who win once or twice by this method are almost sure to lose) Tj T*
(everything sooner or later in an effort to do the same thing again. Your) Tj T*
(chances are not much better than if you gambled at Monte Carlo. The) Tj T*
(chances in buying manipulated stocks are invariably against the) Tj T*
(outsider.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There always is so much publicity about these very active speculative) Tj T*
(stocks that the public is attracted towards them. Newspapers and) Tj T*
(brokers' market letters give altogether too much space to them. Such) Tj T*
(stocks sell far too high, and when the break comes, it brings ruinous) Tj T*
(losses to many people.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On the other hand, by following a conservative course, you really have a) Tj T*
(chance to make large profits with a minimum risk. We are giving below) Tj T*
(sixteen stocks that we recommended in our Advisory Letter of February) Tj T*
(14th, 1922, with the approximate prices of them then and the approximate) Tj T*
(prices on March 31st.[2] In arriving at these prices, we took the) Tj T*
(closing prices on February 13th and on March 31st, and omitted the) Tj T*
(fractions. We recommended only sixteen stocks on that date, and you will) Tj T*
(see that every one of them made substantial gains.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                                 Approximate     Approximate) Tj T*
(                                    Price           Price) Tj T*
(         Stock                  Feb. 14, 1922   Mar. 31, 1922   Profit) Tj T*
