(six, because they were more speculative and would have been more) Tj T*
(affected by a reaction in the market. To buy ten shares of each on that) Tj T*
(margin basis would have required a little less than $3,500, but let us) Tj T*
(suppose you put up $3,500. After allowing for buying and selling) Tj T*
(commissions and interest on the balance of $6,550, but crediting you) Tj T*
(with dividends paid, your profit would be about 32% or at the rate of) Tj T*
(about 250% per annum.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Of course, we do not claim that by following the conservative course we) Tj T*
(advise, you always will make such large profits, although you might do) Tj T*
(just as well as that if you took advantage of some of the opportunities) Tj T*
(so frequently to be found in the market; but keen discrimination in what) Tj T*
(you buy always is necessary. However, let us suppose you made annual) Tj T*
(profits of one-fifth the above amount, or 50%, which is easily possible) Tj T*
(without taking the risks that are usually taken in stock speculating. If) Tj T*
(you invested $1000 and made 50% profit per annum, reinvesting your) Tj T*
(profit at the same rate each year for twenty years, you would have more) Tj T*
(than THREE MILLION DOLLARS.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When there is a possibility of making such enormous profits as that by) Tj T*
(following careful methods, surely there is no argument in favor of) Tj T*
(taking the extreme risks that people do take in buying the highly) Tj T*
(speculative stocks, the prices of which are put up for the purpose of) Tj T*
(unloading them on the public. Ten of the stocks we selected in the above) Tj T*
(list were dividend payers, and while the other six were not, they were) Tj T*
(considered worth much more than their market prices, and the list as a) Tj T*
(whole was conceded by conservative people as a safe one to buy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Very frequently we are able to recommend a list of stocks that we) Tj T*
(believe will yield equally large profits, but the stocks you should buy) Tj T*
(are not the ones that are the most active nor the ones that are) Tj T*
(mentioned most frequently in the financial news and brokers' market) Tj T*
(letters. The stocks that most people buy are usually the very stocks) Tj T*
(that should be left alone. The stocks you should buy are usually the) Tj T*
(ones you hear very little about.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There is only one SAFE way to speculate, and that is to be guided by a) Tj T*
(knowledge of the fundamental conditions of each stock and also of the) Tj T*
(industries they represent. There are several large organizations giving) Tj T*
(information of this kind, and those who have been guided by the) Tj T*
(fundamental statistics issued by them, almost invariably have made money) Tj T*
(in stock speculating. The value of that kind of service has been) Tj T*
(thoroughly demonstrated beyond any question. However, a subscription for) Tj T*
(the service of most of these organizations costs more than the average) Tj T*
(person can afford to pay. Usually it is anywhere from $100 to $1,000 a) Tj T*
(year.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We are giving a service for the purpose of guiding our clients to) Tj T*
(successful speculation for a fee of only $25 a year, $15 for six months,) Tj T*
(or $10 for three months. For this fee we tell you what stocks to buy,) Tj T*
(when to buy, and when to sell. We send you our recommendations at least) Tj T*
(twice a month, but send you additional Advisory Letters and lists) Tj T*
